sequenceDiagram
  %% Non-default container cleanup. Conn admission precedes this forced engine; CLI admission keeps its existing rules.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:destroy
  %% kind: instance.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: instance:destroy<br/>INSTANCE --yes --force
  %% path: main
  %%> Conn admission:
  %%> - POST /api/v1/conn/instances/ID/destroy requires an Idempotency-Key and acknowledge_unsaved as a JSON boolean
  %%> - the caller needs access to the Instance's Node; a missing Instance is 404
  %%> - a default answers 409 instance.default_protected; a host checkout answers 409 instance.not_container
  %%> - without acknowledgement, answer 409 instance.unsaved_work with unknown state and null counts; no container Git observations exist yet
  %%> - these refusals change no Schedule, Route, database, pairing, environment or Operation, and never probe the container
  %%> - acknowledged removal uses this same engine with force=true; all existing engine blockers keep their codes
  %%> - the same key and request returns the same Operation with 202, including after Instance deletion; a changed request is an idempotency conflict
  %%> CLI requirements:
  %%> - Node access to the Instance's Node and no other lifecycle Operation holds the Instance
  %%> - this slice supports a non-default container Instance, cloned or migrated; the Instance named `default` remains unavailable
  %%> - `--force` is required until guarded removal is built; no work or turn check runs
  alt container default
    %% path: default-unavailable
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>operation.kind_unavailable
  else clone without --force
    %% path: force-required
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>force required
    %%> Code:
    %%> - `instance.container_destroy_force_required`
  else forced clone
    %% path: admitted
    Note over GW: Capture removal intent<br/>mark removing
    %%> Result:
    %%> - capture the clone's container identity, Route, Processes and owned databases
    %%> - Conn runs stored blocker checks before calling the engine; the engine keeps its existing Schedule removal and failure boundary
    %%> - keep its runtime row, address and T3 port reserved until terminal success
    %%> - Conn refuses new pairings while the Instance is removing
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-destroy
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
    opt clone has a Route
      %% path: routed
      SW->>N: Withdraw the Route<br/>child route-withdraw
      %%> Caddy publication:
      %%> - on the Node, wait at most 5 s for the publish lock; compare the composed-from SHA-256 with the live file, then validate, rename and reload under that lock
      %%> - a changed base refuses with `caddy.composed_from_live_mismatch`; a busy lock refuses with `caddy.publish_busy`; the live Caddyfile stays unchanged and the normal failure path runs
    end
    opt clone owns server databases
      %% path: server-database
      SW->>N: Drop owned databases<br/>child database-destroy
    end
    SW->>N: Delete the container<br/>Ansible · tags remove
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stops and deletes the clone, its Processes, T3 history, snapshots, storage volume and proxy device
    %%> - deleting T3 retires every session and unused pairing link; no T3 call or new vault key is needed
    %%> - removes its `instance-<id>` ACL from Incus project `default`, its owned UFW rules, its Node repository mirror and its private Node mail activation state
    %%> - checks that the container and storage volume are absent; already absent resources are removed
    %%> - the default and sibling clones stay; a migrated Instance's retained Git directory is untouched and can be purged only by hand
    alt all steps pass
      %% path: succeeded
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      Note over GW: Remove owned records<br/>free T3 port
      %%> Result:
      %%> - remove Instance execution copies and Conn's copies, environment and pairings, even while Conn is disabled
      %%> - delete the Route, Processes, owned database records, runtime row and Instance
      %%> - keep `retained_git_path` and `retained_git_at` in the destroy Operation result so retention stays findable after the Instance row goes
      %%> - deleting the runtime row frees the published T3 port and bridge address
    else a step fails
      %% path: removal-failed
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
      Note over GW: Keep removing<br/>retry saved intent
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - a fresh forced destroy reuses the removal identity and accepts resources already gone
      %%> - after withdrawal the Route stays down; records and the reserved port stay until success
    end
  end
